1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,869
Hi, I'm Ryan Rover.

2
00:00:02,049 --> 00:00:03,362
A new year is coming,

3
00:00:03,362 --> 00:00:04,113
and with it,

4
00:00:04,113 --> 00:00:05,926
a fresh start for your money.

5
00:00:06,106 --> 00:00:09,010
But instead of vague resolutions that fade

6
00:00:09,010 --> 00:00:11,154
by February, I want to give you

7
00:00:11,154 --> 00:00:14,335
something better: thirty simple money rules to

8
00:00:14,335 --> 00:00:15,441
live by in 2027.

9
00:00:15,621 --> 00:00:16,907
Rules you can remember,

10
00:00:16,907 --> 00:00:18,081
rules you can follow,

11
00:00:18,081 --> 00:00:20,093
and rules that work whether you earn

12
00:00:20,093 --> 00:00:22,889
thirty thousand dollars or three hundred thousand.

13
00:00:23,239 --> 00:00:25,375
Why rules instead of goals?

14
00:00:25,555 --> 00:00:27,537
Because goals tell you where you want

15
00:00:27,537 --> 00:00:29,144
to go, but rules tell you what

16
00:00:29,144 --> 00:00:30,001
to do every day.

17
00:00:30,181 --> 00:00:31,853
Rules remove decisions.

18
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:33,885
When you already know your rule,

19
00:00:33,885 --> 00:00:35,736
you don't have to think about it

20
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:36,546
in the moment,

21
00:00:36,546 --> 00:00:38,803
when emotions are high and willpower is

22
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:39,034
low.

23
00:00:39,383 --> 00:00:41,549
We'll go through these thirty rules in

24
00:00:41,549 --> 00:00:43,087
three groups, three angles.

25
00:00:43,267 --> 00:00:45,573
First, ten rules about the numbers:

26
00:00:45,573 --> 00:00:48,010
the targets and ratios that keep your

27
00:00:48,010 --> 00:00:49,130
finances healthy.

28
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:51,672
Second, ten rules about the psychology:

29
00:00:51,672 --> 00:00:53,792
how to think and behave with money.

30
00:00:53,972 --> 00:00:55,684
And third, ten action rules:

31
00:00:55,684 --> 00:00:58,069
the playbook of habits that protect and

32
00:00:58,069 --> 00:00:59,231
grow what you have.

33
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,171
Stay for rule fifteen.

34
00:01:01,351 --> 00:01:02,953
It could protect you from one of

35
00:01:02,953 --> 00:01:05,055
the fastest growing threats to your money.

36
00:01:05,235 --> 00:01:06,941
Let's start with the numbers.

37
00:01:07,292 --> 00:01:10,737
Every January, millions of people make financial

38
00:01:10,737 --> 00:01:11,599
resolutions.

39
00:01:11,779 --> 00:01:12,742
Save more.

40
00:01:12,922 --> 00:01:13,851
Spend less.

41
00:01:14,031 --> 00:01:14,948
Pay off debt.

42
00:01:15,128 --> 00:01:16,159
And by spring,

43
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,147
many have quietly given up.

44
00:01:18,327 --> 00:01:19,906
The problem isn't motivation.

45
00:01:20,086 --> 00:01:21,836
It's that resolutions are vague,

46
00:01:21,836 --> 00:01:23,968
and vague goals give your brain nothing

47
00:01:23,968 --> 00:01:24,788
specific to do.

48
00:01:25,138 --> 00:01:29,642
Psychologists call specific plans implementation intentions.

49
00:01:29,822 --> 00:01:33,065
Research by psychologist Peter Gollwitzer and others

50
00:01:33,065 --> 00:01:35,498
found that people who decide in advance

51
00:01:35,498 --> 00:01:37,806
exactly what they'll do in a specific

52
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:40,550
situation are more likely to follow through.

53
00:01:40,730 --> 00:01:42,194
When X happens,

54
00:01:42,194 --> 00:01:42,878
I do Y.

55
00:01:43,058 --> 00:01:45,020
Money rules work the same way.

56
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:46,792
When a raise arrives,

57
00:01:46,792 --> 00:01:48,214
half goes to savings.

58
00:01:48,394 --> 00:01:50,330
When I want something over one hundred

59
00:01:50,330 --> 00:01:52,063
dollars, I wait forty eight hours.

60
00:01:52,243 --> 00:01:53,651
When the market drops,

61
00:01:53,651 --> 00:01:54,739
I keep investing.

62
00:01:54,919 --> 00:01:57,212
Each rule is a decision made once,

63
00:01:57,212 --> 00:01:59,910
calmly, that protects you in hundreds of

64
00:01:59,910 --> 00:02:00,921
future moments.

65
00:02:01,272 --> 00:02:04,087
Guidelines in this video come from widely

66
00:02:04,087 --> 00:02:07,108
used sources, including the Federal Reserve,

67
00:02:07,108 --> 00:02:09,924
the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau,

68
00:02:09,924 --> 00:02:11,915
the Federal Trade Commission,

69
00:02:11,915 --> 00:02:13,358
the IRS and Fidelity.

70
00:02:13,538 --> 00:02:16,437
Growth examples are stated math and are

71
00:02:16,437 --> 00:02:18,518
illustrations, not promises.

72
00:02:18,698 --> 00:02:20,945
These rules are general guidelines,

73
00:02:20,945 --> 00:02:22,229
not personal advice,

74
00:02:22,229 --> 00:02:24,860
and your situation may call for different

75
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:25,374
numbers.

76
00:02:25,724 --> 00:02:26,385
Angle one.

77
00:02:26,565 --> 00:02:28,284
Ten rules about the numbers.

78
00:02:28,634 --> 00:02:29,377
Rule 1.

79
00:02:29,557 --> 00:02:32,074
Keep 3 to 6 months of essentials

80
00:02:32,074 --> 00:02:32,703
in cash.

81
00:02:33,053 --> 00:02:33,703
Rule one.

82
00:02:33,883 --> 00:02:36,405
Keep three to six months of essential

83
00:02:36,405 --> 00:02:39,200
expenses in a high yield savings account.

84
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:41,409
In recent Federal Reserve surveys,

85
00:02:41,409 --> 00:02:43,557
more than a third of American adults

86
00:02:43,557 --> 00:02:45,884
said they couldn't cover a four hundred

87
00:02:45,884 --> 00:02:47,495
dollar emergency with cash.

88
00:02:47,675 --> 00:02:50,603
An emergency fund is what keeps surprises

89
00:02:50,603 --> 00:02:51,960
from becoming debt.

90
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:54,147
If you're starting from zero,

91
00:02:54,147 --> 00:02:56,175
start with five hundred dollars,

92
00:02:56,175 --> 00:02:57,315
then one thousand,

93
00:02:57,315 --> 00:02:58,265
then one month.

94
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:00,744
Every stage protects you more than the

95
00:03:00,744 --> 00:03:01,046
last.

96
00:03:01,226 --> 00:03:03,908
In 2027, make this your first priority

97
00:03:03,908 --> 00:03:05,673
if you don't have it yet.

98
00:03:06,023 --> 00:03:07,710
How to apply it in 2027:

99
00:03:07,710 --> 00:03:10,662
open a separate high yield savings account

100
00:03:10,662 --> 00:03:12,208
if you don't have one,

101
00:03:12,208 --> 00:03:13,825
name it Emergency Fund,

102
00:03:13,825 --> 00:03:16,426
and set an automatic transfer for the

103
00:03:16,426 --> 00:03:17,621
day after payday.

104
00:03:17,801 --> 00:03:19,543
Then put a share of your tax

105
00:03:19,543 --> 00:03:21,098
refund in it this spring.

106
00:03:21,278 --> 00:03:23,133
Those two moves alone can get many

107
00:03:23,133 --> 00:03:25,260
people to their first thousand dollars.

108
00:03:25,611 --> 00:03:26,470
Rule 2.

109
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:29,355
Save at least 15% for retirement.

110
00:03:29,705 --> 00:03:30,564
Rule two.

111
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:33,175
Save at least fifteen percent of your

112
00:03:33,175 --> 00:03:35,015
gross income for retirement,

113
00:03:35,015 --> 00:03:36,920
including any employer match.

114
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:39,173
It's one of the most common guidelines

115
00:03:39,173 --> 00:03:40,537
from retirement planners.

116
00:03:40,717 --> 00:03:41,956
If you start late,

117
00:03:41,956 --> 00:03:42,714
aim higher.

118
00:03:43,064 --> 00:03:45,687
If fifteen percent isn't possible yet,

119
00:03:45,687 --> 00:03:48,725
raise your contribution by one percent every

120
00:03:48,725 --> 00:03:49,484
few months.

121
00:03:49,664 --> 00:03:52,822
Many workplace plans offer automatic increases.

122
00:03:53,002 --> 00:03:53,682
Turn them on,

123
00:03:53,682 --> 00:03:55,304
and in a couple of years you'll

124
00:03:55,304 --> 00:03:57,448
get there without feeling a sudden pinch.

125
00:03:57,799 --> 00:03:59,665
How to apply it in 2027:

126
00:03:59,665 --> 00:04:02,777
log into your retirement plan in January

127
00:04:02,777 --> 00:04:06,355
and write down your current contribution rate.

128
00:04:06,535 --> 00:04:08,503
If it's below fifteen percent,

129
00:04:08,503 --> 00:04:10,273
raise it by at least one or

130
00:04:10,273 --> 00:04:11,257
two points now,

131
00:04:11,257 --> 00:04:13,815
and schedule another increase for July.

132
00:04:13,995 --> 00:04:15,656
If you get a raise this year,

133
00:04:15,656 --> 00:04:17,604
send half of it to your retirement

134
00:04:17,604 --> 00:04:18,348
contribution.

135
00:04:18,699 --> 00:04:19,697
Rule 3.

136
00:04:19,877 --> 00:04:21,711
Never leave the match on the table.

137
00:04:22,062 --> 00:04:22,967
Rule three.

138
00:04:23,147 --> 00:04:26,237
If your employer matches retirement contributions,

139
00:04:26,237 --> 00:04:28,709
always contribute enough to get the full

140
00:04:28,709 --> 00:04:29,080
match.

141
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:31,345
On a sixty thousand dollar salary,

142
00:04:31,345 --> 00:04:33,492
a four percent match is twenty four

143
00:04:33,492 --> 00:04:34,902
hundred dollars a year.

144
00:04:35,082 --> 00:04:36,999
Not taking it is turning down a

145
00:04:36,999 --> 00:04:37,369
raise.

146
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,247
Check your plan's match formula and vesting

147
00:04:40,247 --> 00:04:41,423
schedule this month.

148
00:04:41,603 --> 00:04:43,540
If you're not getting the full match,

149
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:45,478
fixing it might be the single highest

150
00:04:45,478 --> 00:04:47,048
return move you make all year.

151
00:04:47,399 --> 00:04:49,110
How to apply it in 2027:

152
00:04:49,110 --> 00:04:51,178
if you change jobs this year,

153
00:04:51,178 --> 00:04:53,745
ask about the match during the offer

154
00:04:53,745 --> 00:04:55,955
process, and enroll on day one.

155
00:04:56,135 --> 00:04:59,429
Some employers have waiting periods or require

156
00:04:59,429 --> 00:05:00,431
you to opt in.

157
00:05:00,611 --> 00:05:02,808
Don't let months of free money slip

158
00:05:02,808 --> 00:05:04,314
by because of paperwork.

159
00:05:04,665 --> 00:05:05,338
Rule 4.

160
00:05:05,518 --> 00:05:08,153
Pay off any debt above about 8%.

161
00:05:08,504 --> 00:05:09,409
Rule four.

162
00:05:09,589 --> 00:05:12,318
Treat debt above roughly eight percent interest

163
00:05:12,318 --> 00:05:13,246
as an emergency.

164
00:05:13,426 --> 00:05:16,033
Credit card rates have often averaged above

165
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:17,913
twenty percent in recent years,

166
00:05:17,913 --> 00:05:19,974
according to Federal Reserve data.

167
00:05:20,154 --> 00:05:22,393
Paying off a twenty two percent card

168
00:05:22,393 --> 00:05:24,818
is like earning a guaranteed twenty two

169
00:05:24,818 --> 00:05:25,750
percent return.

170
00:05:26,101 --> 00:05:28,206
List your debts by interest rate,

171
00:05:28,206 --> 00:05:29,992
pay minimums on all of them,

172
00:05:29,992 --> 00:05:32,161
and attack the highest rate first.

173
00:05:32,341 --> 00:05:33,427
When one is gone,

174
00:05:33,427 --> 00:05:35,406
roll its payment into the next.

175
00:05:35,756 --> 00:05:37,647
How to apply it in 2027:

176
00:05:37,647 --> 00:05:40,249
write every debt on one page with

177
00:05:40,249 --> 00:05:43,244
its balance, rate and minimum payment.

178
00:05:43,424 --> 00:05:44,887
Circle the highest rate.

179
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:46,553
That's your target for the year.

180
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:49,557
Set an automatic extra payment toward it,

181
00:05:49,557 --> 00:05:51,417
even fifty dollars a month,

182
00:05:51,417 --> 00:05:52,933
and add any windfalls.

183
00:05:53,283 --> 00:05:54,258
Rule 5.

184
00:05:54,438 --> 00:05:57,810
Keep housing around 30% of gross income

185
00:05:57,810 --> 00:05:58,501
or less.

186
00:05:58,852 --> 00:05:59,769
Rule five.

187
00:05:59,949 --> 00:06:02,753
A common guideline is to keep housing

188
00:06:02,753 --> 00:06:05,633
costs at or below about thirty percent

189
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:06,845
of gross income.

190
00:06:07,025 --> 00:06:09,839
Housing is usually the largest expense in

191
00:06:09,839 --> 00:06:12,515
any budget, around a third of household

192
00:06:12,515 --> 00:06:13,956
spending in BLS data.

193
00:06:14,136 --> 00:06:16,411
Getting this one decision right makes every

194
00:06:16,411 --> 00:06:17,364
other goal easier.

195
00:06:17,714 --> 00:06:18,941
In expensive cities,

196
00:06:18,941 --> 00:06:21,150
that may not be possible right away.

197
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:23,494
If so, look for ways to bring

198
00:06:23,494 --> 00:06:24,837
it down over time:

199
00:06:24,837 --> 00:06:27,673
a roommate, a cheaper unit at renewal,

200
00:06:27,673 --> 00:06:29,016
or a smaller home.

201
00:06:29,196 --> 00:06:31,327
Every hundred dollars saved on housing is

202
00:06:31,327 --> 00:06:32,470
twelve hundred a year.

203
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:34,618
How to apply it in 2027:

204
00:06:34,618 --> 00:06:36,866
if your lease is up this year,

205
00:06:36,866 --> 00:06:40,763
compare at least three alternatives before renewing,

206
00:06:40,763 --> 00:06:42,711
and use them to negotiate.

207
00:06:42,891 --> 00:06:43,594
If you own,

208
00:06:43,594 --> 00:06:46,598
check whether your property taxes and insurance

209
00:06:46,598 --> 00:06:49,346
have risen and shop your homeowners policy.

210
00:06:49,526 --> 00:06:52,626
Small housing savings repeat every single month.

211
00:06:52,977 --> 00:06:53,975
Rule 6.

212
00:06:54,155 --> 00:06:56,082
Use the rule of 72.

213
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:57,512
Rule six.

214
00:06:57,692 --> 00:06:59,987
Divide seventy two by an interest rate

215
00:06:59,987 --> 00:07:02,101
to estimate how many years it takes

216
00:07:02,101 --> 00:07:03,068
money to double.

217
00:07:03,248 --> 00:07:04,495
At seven percent,

218
00:07:04,495 --> 00:07:06,916
money doubles in about ten years.

219
00:07:07,096 --> 00:07:08,252
At ten percent,

220
00:07:08,252 --> 00:07:09,639
about seven years.

221
00:07:09,989 --> 00:07:11,393
It works for debt too.

222
00:07:11,573 --> 00:07:14,255
At twenty two percent credit card interest,

223
00:07:14,255 --> 00:07:16,687
an unpaid balance can roughly double in

224
00:07:16,687 --> 00:07:18,620
about three and a half years if

225
00:07:18,620 --> 00:07:20,304
interest keeps compounding.

226
00:07:20,484 --> 00:07:22,907
Knowing this one number helps you understand

227
00:07:22,907 --> 00:07:24,339
both sides of compounding.

228
00:07:24,689 --> 00:07:26,674
How to apply it in 2027:

229
00:07:26,674 --> 00:07:29,156
use the rule of seventy two on

230
00:07:29,156 --> 00:07:30,644
your own accounts.

231
00:07:30,824 --> 00:07:33,249
What rate is your savings account earning,

232
00:07:33,249 --> 00:07:34,981
and how long until it doubles?

233
00:07:35,161 --> 00:07:37,065
What rate is your credit card charging?

234
00:07:37,245 --> 00:07:39,414
Seeing those two numbers side by side

235
00:07:39,414 --> 00:07:41,291
is often the push people need to

236
00:07:41,291 --> 00:07:43,050
move money to the right place.

237
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,131
Rule 7.

238
00:07:44,311 --> 00:07:46,946
Keep investment fees as low as possible.

239
00:07:47,297 --> 00:07:48,214
Rule seven.

240
00:07:48,394 --> 00:07:50,947
Pay attention to the expense ratio,

241
00:07:50,947 --> 00:07:52,771
the yearly fee on a fund.

242
00:07:52,951 --> 00:07:55,671
Many broad index funds charge well under

243
00:07:55,671 --> 00:07:57,235
a quarter of a percent.

244
00:07:57,415 --> 00:08:00,866
Some actively managed funds charge one percent

245
00:08:00,866 --> 00:08:01,467
or more.

246
00:08:01,817 --> 00:08:03,082
The difference adds up.

247
00:08:03,262 --> 00:08:05,803
Investing five hundred dollars a month for

248
00:08:05,803 --> 00:08:08,102
thirty years, a six percent net return

249
00:08:08,102 --> 00:08:10,279
could grow to about five hundred two

250
00:08:10,279 --> 00:08:11,308
thousand dollars.

251
00:08:11,488 --> 00:08:13,277
A five percent net return,

252
00:08:13,277 --> 00:08:16,099
the same investment with one percent more

253
00:08:16,099 --> 00:08:19,197
in fees, about four hundred sixteen thousand.

254
00:08:19,377 --> 00:08:22,003
That one percent costs roughly eighty six

255
00:08:22,003 --> 00:08:23,092
thousand dollars.

256
00:08:23,442 --> 00:08:25,616
How to apply it in 2027:

257
00:08:25,616 --> 00:08:28,696
look up the expense ratio of every

258
00:08:28,696 --> 00:08:29,874
fund you own.

259
00:08:30,054 --> 00:08:32,333
It's listed on your account website or

260
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,293
the fund's page.

261
00:08:33,473 --> 00:08:35,482
If any fund charges much more than

262
00:08:35,482 --> 00:08:36,900
a comparable index fund,

263
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,732
consider whether it's worth it.

264
00:08:38,912 --> 00:08:40,961
Check for account fees too,

265
00:08:40,961 --> 00:08:44,148
like advisory fees or maintenance charges.

266
00:08:44,498 --> 00:08:47,011
Five hundred dollars a month for thirty

267
00:08:47,011 --> 00:08:49,202
years, at a six percent net return

268
00:08:49,202 --> 00:08:51,651
versus five percent after an extra one

269
00:08:51,651 --> 00:08:52,683
percent in fees.

270
00:08:53,033 --> 00:08:53,787
Rule 8.

271
00:08:53,967 --> 00:08:56,579
Keep total car costs under control.

272
00:08:56,930 --> 00:08:57,580
Rule eight.

273
00:08:57,760 --> 00:09:00,508
A popular guideline is the twenty four

274
00:09:00,508 --> 00:09:03,185
ten rule: put at least twenty percent

275
00:09:03,185 --> 00:09:05,716
down, finance for no more than four

276
00:09:05,716 --> 00:09:08,031
years, and keep total car costs,

277
00:09:08,031 --> 00:09:10,707
including payment, insurance and gas,

278
00:09:10,707 --> 00:09:13,166
under ten percent of gross income.

279
00:09:13,346 --> 00:09:15,724
Many people use a looser version,

280
00:09:15,724 --> 00:09:17,526
but the idea is the same.

281
00:09:17,876 --> 00:09:19,619
Cars lose value quickly,

282
00:09:19,619 --> 00:09:22,090
especially in the first few years.

283
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,612
Buying a reliable used car and keeping

284
00:09:24,612 --> 00:09:26,152
it for a long time is one

285
00:09:26,152 --> 00:09:28,925
of the most consistent wealth building habits

286
00:09:28,925 --> 00:09:29,480
there is.

287
00:09:29,830 --> 00:09:31,736
